 is isosceles with \\( \\mathrm{AC} = \\mathrm{BC} \\).\n   - Point \\( \\mathrm{E} \\) is on the base \\( \\mathrm{AC} \\).\n   - Points \\( \\mathrm{K} \\) and \\( \\mathrm{M} \\) are on sides \\( \\mathrm{AB} \\) and \\( \\mathrm{BC} \\) respectively.\n   - Line segment \\( \\mathrm{KE} \\) is parallel to \\( \\mathrm{BC} \\) and \\( \\mathrm{EM} \\) is parallel to \\( \\mathrm{AB} \\).\n\n2. **Using parallel properties**:\n   - Since \\( \\mathrm{KE} \\parallel \\mathrm{BC} \\), \\( \\mathrm{BKEC} \\) is a trapezoid.\n   - Since \\( \\mathrm{B} \\) and \\( \\mathrm{E} \\) are connected by \\( \\mathrm{KE} \\), and it\u2019s parallel to the opposite side \\( \\mathrm{BC} \\), we have similar triangles \\( \\mathrm{AKE} \\sim \\mathrm{ABC} \\).\n\n3. **Ratio calculation for similar triangles**:\n   - Given \\( \\mathrm{BM}: \\mathrm{EM} = 2:3 \\), we use the proportion to find the lengths.\n   - Consider the whole side \\( \\mathrm{BC} \\). Let \\( \\mathrm{BC} = x + y \\).\n   - Since \\( \\mathrm{BM}: \\mathrm{EM} = 2:3 \\), we have \\( \\mathrm{BM} = 2k \\) and \\( \\mathrm{EM} = 3k \\), making \\( \\mathrm{BC} = 5k \\).\n\n4. **Area proportion and similarity**:\n   - The ratio \\( \\frac{\\mathrm{KE}}{\\mathrm{BC}} = \\frac{2}{5} \\):\n     \\[\n     \\frac{\\mathrm{KE}}{\\mathrm{BC}} = \\frac{2x}{5x} = \\frac{2}{5}\n     \\]\n   - Similarly, \\( \\frac{\\mathrm{MC}}{\\mathrm{BC}} = \\frac{3x}{5x} = \\frac{3}{5} \\).\n\n5. **Calculate areas using the side proportions**:\n   - The area of triangle \\( \\mathrm{ABC} \\), denote as \\( S_{\\mathrm{ABC}} \\), is composed of the areas of triangles \\( \\mathrm{AKE} \\) and \\( \\mathrm{EMC} \\), and the quadrilateral \\( \\mathrm{KEMC} \\).\n   - Since \\( \\mathrm{AKE} \\sim \\mathrm{ABC} \\) and they are similar by the ratio \\( \\frac{2}{5} \\), the areas scale by the square of the similarity ratio:\n     \\[\n     S_{\\mathrm{AKE}} = \\left(\\frac{2}{5}\\right)^2 S_{\\mathrm{ABC}} = \\frac{4}{25} S_{\\mathrm{ABC}}\n     \\]\n   - Similarly for \\( \\mathrm{EMC} \\):\n     \\[\n     S_{\\mathrm{EMC}} = \\left(\\frac{3}{5}\\right)^2 S_{\\mathrm{ABC}} = \\frac{9}{25} S_{\\mathrm{ABC}}\n     \\]\n\n6. **Total area computation**:\n    \\[\n    S_{\\mathrm{KEM}} = \\frac{1}{2} S_{\\mathrm{KEMC}} = \\frac{1}{2} \\left( S_{\\mathrm{ABC}} - S_{\\mathrm{AKE}} - S_{\\mathrm{EMC}} \\right)\n    \\]\n    Plugging in the values:\n    \\[\n    S_{\\mathrm{KEM}} = \\frac{1}{2} \\left( 1 - \\frac{4}{25} - \\frac{9}{25} \\right) S_{\\mathrm{ABC}}\n    \\]\n    Simplifying the fractional terms:\n    \\[\n    S_{\\mathrm{KEM}} = \\frac{1}{2} \\left( 1 - \\frac{13}{25} \\right) S_{\\mathrm{ABC}}\n    \\]\n    \\[\n    S_{\\mathrm{KEM}} = \\frac{1}{2} \\left( \\frac{25}{25} - \\frac{13}{25} \\right) S_{\\mathrm{ABC}}\n    \\]\n    \\[\n    S_{\\mathrm{KEM}} = \\frac{1}{2} \\left( \\frac{12}{25} \\right) S_{\\mathrm{ABC}}\n    \\]\n    \\[\n    S_{\\mathrm{KEM}} = \\frac{6}{25} S_{\\mathrm{ABC}}\n    \\]\n\n### Conclusion:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{6}{25}}\n\\]", "domain": "math", "source": "numina_math", "test_cases": null, "starter_code": null}]